## Recent Recalls on the Rise  
This year alone, there have been 714 food recalls--a staggering number that surpasses the total count of other years recorded. The month of June 2026 alone saw 213 recalls, which makes it the highest single-month count in recent memory. Of particular note are the 181 Class I recalls this year, items that pose a serious risk of harm to consumers.  

## Brand Spotlight: Moonlight Packing Corporation  
One of the most alarming patterns is the repeat offenders. Moonlight Packing Corporation has racked up an unprecedented 11 Class I recalls this year. Their products, ranging from fruits to packaged goods, have consistently been flagged for serious safety issues. In fact, Moonlight has earned an overall grade of "F" in our rankings, reflecting pervasive issues in their production processes.  

## The Weekly Top Recalls  
Here are some notable recalls from the past week:  
- **MID DOLCIARIA SRL**: Crunchy Cannoli Gluten Free recalled due to unapproved coloring agents E140 and E141.  
- **Dkiru LLC**: Adndale Magnesium Glycinate Gummies recalled for containing undeclared melatonin.  
- **Greenworld Food Express (USA) LLC**: Al Yaman Halawa Extra Pistachio possibly contaminated with Salmonella, receiving a Class I recall.  

## The Takeaway  
The food industry remains fraught with hazards, from contamination to mislabeling. While strides have been made, the uptick in recalls suggests deeper systemic concerns. For a safer future, stricter enforcement and accountability are imperative.
